From 732f33be360ffb5e1f7b4a17ccecc41a90a0e9d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:28:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [libc] add Linux headers sys/epoll.h and sys/inotify.h

Event-driven Linux code (network daemons, resolvers, file watchers)
includes <sys/epoll.h> or <sys/inotify.h>, and parsing it currently
stops with "fatal error: sys/epoll.h: No such file or directory".

Add both headers, in the style of sys/sendfile.h and sys/prctl.h:
- the Linux constants (EPOLL*, EPOLL_CTL_*, EPOLL_CLOEXEC, IN_*,
  IN_CLOEXEC, IN_NONBLOCK) with the Linux values;
- struct epoll_event, packed on x86_64 as in glibc (12 bytes), the
  epoll_data union, and struct inotify_event;
- epoll_create, epoll_create1, epoll_ctl, epoll_wait, epoll_pwait,
  inotify_init, inotify_init1, inotify_add_watch and inotify_rm_watch,
  with minimal contracts: validity of the descriptors and buffers,
  assigns clauses, the -1 error result, and for epoll_wait/epoll_pwait
  the same full/partial behaviors as read(). The kernel-side interest
  and watch lists are not modelled (//missing: comments).

Add both headers to share/libc/__fc_libc.h and tests/libc/fc_libc.c, and
one Eva test per header under tests/libc. The fc_libc.0 and fc_libc.2
oracles gain the two include lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
